		(uuid "8c95cdc0-f1df-4880-aa78-9c85d78fd888")
	)
	(text "Buttons can be whatever, but I used tall ones found here:\n\nhttps://www.digikey.ca/en/products/detail/e-switch/tl3301pf160qg/1756542\n\n\n\nAlso, for resistor it may be worth using an array. I designed this before I knew what R-arr's looked like. \nHere's a link to one I found that's 10k and has 8 resistors:\n\nhttps://www.digikey.ca/en/products/detail/panasonic-industry/EXB-2HV103JV/285331\n\n\n\nAdditionally, instead of having FLOOR1, FLOOR2, ..., it might be worth using a MUX here to make 8 inputs into 3 outputs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.352 73.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b773dd47-bb9a-4f40-a072-620c0c872b00")
	)
	(text "From any\nESP GPIO\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.862 124.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "c467a3e8-6c24-42b6-9075-cd8d8b2175b1")
	)
	(text "Floor 1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 34.798 42.418 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
		)
		(uuid "c6b2818f-e2e4-4744-9b7b-5a8b265d482b")
	)
	(text "You'll probably have to add a footprint for this one... (74HCT595)\n\nThere are SOIC-16 and TSSOP-16 options available on DigiKey. Links below:\n\nTSSOP-16:\nhttps://www.digikey.ca/en/products/detail/nexperia-usa-inc/74HCT595PW-118/763165\n\n\nSOIC-16:\nhttps://www.digikey.ca/en/products/detail/nexperia-usa-inc/74HCT595D-118/763163\n\n\nSo use whatever footprint you prefer"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 161.036 120.396 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "dd4e6662-d067-4a36-8e45-b16e6c115972")
	)
